    "primary": {
     "type": "TextChapter",
     "page_section_element_title": [],
     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Use Switches for binary options where users need to choose between two mutually exclusive states like on/off, enabled/disabled, or active/inactive. Ensure Switches are clearly labeled to indicate what each state represents.",
       "spans": [],
       "direction": "ltr"
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "Differentiate between Switches and Checkboxes: Switches are ideal for toggling between two distinct states, while Checkboxes are suitable for selecting one or more options from a list of choices. Toggling a Switch typically triggers an action instantly upon interaction, while a checkbox usually requires confirmation.",
